{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Analytic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.boost_factor_dictionary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.boost_factor_dictionary","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.lean#L112-L127","doc":"**The qou-yh67 boost factor IS the object choice.** For a real deformation\n`r ≠ 0`, the ratio of the imaginary face to the complex-volume scale `κ_pot·r²`\nis exactly `1` for the complex volume `𝔙` and exactly `2` for the full\npotential `Φ`. So the opaque `A ∈ {1, 2}` (#4541) is precisely the binary\n\"observable = complex volume `𝔙` (A=1, `c=1`) vs full NZ potential `Φ = 2𝔙`\n(A=2, `c=√2`)\" — the presence/absence of the NZ ½. This does NOT decide which\nthe physical `S` inherits (open, bean qou-yh67); it only fixes that the choice\nis a genuine object choice with the two clean values `1` and `2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.imFullPotential_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.imFullPotential_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.lean#L104-L110","doc":"On the real substrate ray (`u = r : ℝ`): `Im Φ(r) = κ_shape·r² = 2·(κ_pot·r²)`.\nThe boost factor relative to the complex-volume scale `κ_pot·r²` is exactly\n`2` for the full potential. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.imComplexVolume_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.imComplexVolume_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.lean#L99-L102","doc":"On the real substrate ray (`u = r : ℝ`): `Im 𝔙(r) = κ_pot·r²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.imFullPotential_eq_two_mul_imComplexVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.imFullPotential_eq_two_mul_imComplexVolume","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.lean#L89-L97","doc":"**`Φ = 2·𝔙` on the imaginary face (the object dictionary).** For every `u`,\n`Im Φ(u) = 2·Im 𝔙(u)`: the full NZ potential is exactly twice the complex\nvolume. The two qou-yh67 candidate coefficients are ONE geometric object\n(`𝔙`, the Chern–Simons invariant) and TWICE it (`Φ`, the un-halved longitude\nintegral) — related by the NZ ½, not by a free convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.imFullPotential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.imFullPotential","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.lean#L85-L87","doc":"**Im of the full NZ potential `Φ = 2𝔙`** (the raw longitude integral):\n`Im Φ(u) = κ_shape·(Re²u − Im²u)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.imComplexVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.imComplexVolume","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.lean#L81-L83","doc":"**Im of the complex volume `𝔙`** (the physical Chern–Simons invariant):\n`Im 𝔙(u) = κ_pot·(Re²u − Im²u)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.kappaFull_eq_two_mul_kappaCV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.kappaFull_eq_two_mul_kappaCV","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.lean#L75-L79","doc":"**The Neumann–Zagier ½.** `κ_shape = 2·κ_pot`: the full-potential coefficient\nis exactly twice the complex-volume coefficient (`Φ = 2·𝔙`). Falsifiable: the\nratio could have been any real; it is exactly 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.kappaFull_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.kappaFull_pos","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.lean#L73-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.kappaCV_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.kappaCV_pos","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.kappaFull","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.kappaFull","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.lean#L65-L70","doc":"**Full-potential coefficient `κ_shape = √3/2`.** The imaginary-part coefficient\nof the FULL NZ potential `Φ(u) = ∫₀ᵘ log(−L) dt` — the raw A-polynomial\nlongitude integral WITHOUT the NZ ½ (A-polynomial ground truth,\n`docs/audits/2026-07-27-nzImVolume-sincos-convention-bug.md`). Same constant as\n`QOU.MassTheory.nzReVolume` / `QOU.QBeta.ArgUPhaseBranchSelection.nzImVolume`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.kappaCV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.kappaCV","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential.lean#L59-L63","doc":"**Complex-volume coefficient `κ_pot = √3/4`.** The imaginary-part coefficient\nof the deformed COMPLEX VOLUME `𝔙 = Φ/2` — the genuine Chern–Simons invariant,\ncarrying the Neumann–Zagier ½ (`∂𝔙/∂u = ½·v`). Same constant as\n`QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.cuspModulus`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}